1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,750
Move your index finger sideways, then try the same movement near your palm.
先横向移动食指，再在靠近掌心的位置重复这个动作。

2
00:00:06,530 --> 00:00:11,630
The robot should respond predictably, without suddenly becoming stiff or oversensitive.
机器人应响应可预测，不该突然迟钝或过度敏感。

3
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:16,010
A learned retargeter therefore needs more than one convincing hand pose.
因此，学习式重定向需要的不只是一张看起来相似的手势。

4
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,970
It needs a useful mapping across the motions you actually perform.
它要在你实际会做的动作范围内，建立有效映射。

5
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:24,070
In this chapter, we follow three approaches to learning that mapping.
这一章，我们沿着三种方法，拆开这个映射如何被学会。

6
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:29,270
The key questions are where supervision comes from, and what remains outside the network.
关键是监督信号从哪里来，以及哪些问题仍在网络之外。

7
00:00:29,856 --> 00:00:35,156
An online optimizer starts with a human pose and searches for suitable robot joints.
在线优化器拿到人手姿态后，现场搜索合适的机器人关节角。

8
00:00:35,436 --> 00:00:40,096
A neural retargeter performs most of that computational work during training instead.
神经网络重定向则把大量计算工作，提前放到了训练阶段。

9
00:00:40,396 --> 00:00:44,616
At deployment, its learned weights turn a new input into an immediate prediction.
部署时，已经学好的参数把新输入变成一次直接预测。

10
00:00:44,896 --> 00:00:49,516
This is amortization: earlier computation is shared across many later queries.
这叫摊销：前期计算被后面大量查询共同分担。

11
00:00:49,796 --> 00:00:54,936
The optimization objective still matters, because it defines what the network learns to prefer.
优化目标仍然重要，因为它决定网络会偏好什么样的解。

12
00:00:55,296 --> 00:00:59,676
Fast predictions can still violate constraints that training only softly encourages.
快速预测也可能违反那些只在训练中被软性鼓励的约束。

13
00:01:00,301 --> 00:01:05,341
Robotic Telekinesis starts with a single color camera looking at the operator.
Robotic Telekinesis 从一台朝向操作者的彩色摄像头开始。

14
00:01:05,881 --> 00:01:10,881
In the original figure, the upper branch estimates the human hand and retargets its pose.
原图上方分支先估计人手，再把姿态映射给机器人手。

15
00:01:11,381 --> 00:01:15,621
The lower branch separately estimates body motion to position the robot arm.
下方分支单独估计人体运动，用来确定机械臂位置。

16
00:01:16,041 --> 00:01:21,601
The hand network receives estimated hand parameters and produces sixteen Allegro joint angles.
手部网络输入估计的人手参数，输出 Allegro 的十六个关节角。

17
00:01:22,181 --> 00:01:27,066
Those angles are targets, followed by filtering, limits, and the robot control stack.
这些角度是目标，之后还有滤波、限幅和机器人的控制系统。

18
00:01:27,081 --> 00:01:33,101
The camera, pose estimator, retargeter, and physical controller therefore have different jobs.
所以，摄像头、姿态估计、重定向和物理控制器各有不同职责。

19
00:01:33,708 --> 00:01:39,308
The training images provide human poses, but not a unique matching robot pose.
训练图像提供人手姿态，却没有唯一对应的机器人姿态。

20
00:01:39,868 --> 00:01:44,928
Robotic Telekinesis uses a geometric energy to judge each predicted configuration.
Robotic Telekinesis 用几何能量评价每个预测出的构型。

21
00:01:45,788 --> 00:01:49,728
Relative landmark vectors should agree after accounting for different hand proportions.
考虑两种手的尺寸差异后，关键点之间的相对向量应尽量一致。

22
00:01:50,348 --> 00:01:55,328
Differentiable forward kinematics connects robot joints to those geometric relationships.
可微正向运动学把机器人关节角连接到这些几何关系。

23
00:01:56,008 --> 00:01:59,888
Gradients then tell the network how to reduce the energy on its next update.
梯度再告诉网络，下一次更新怎样降低这个能量。

24
00:02:00,228 --> 00:02:05,268
No paired robot labels does not mean no supervision; the objective supplies the supervision.
没有配对机器人标签，不等于没有监督；监督来自设计好的目标。

25
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:09,620
Look at the blue forward arrows in this original training diagram.
看原论文训练图里，蓝色箭头表示的前向计算。

26
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:15,700
The retargeter predicts joints; a separate classifier estimates self-collision probability.
重定向网络预测关节角，另一个分类器估计自碰撞概率。

27
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:21,180
That classifier was trained using robot configurations labeled by a collision checker.
这个分类器先用机器人构型训练，标签由碰撞检测器生成。

28
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:26,520
During retargeter training, it stays fixed while the red gradient arrows update the mapper.
训练重定向网络时，分类器保持固定，红色梯度箭头更新映射网络。

29
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:31,340
This makes collision avoidance differentiable enough to influence the training process.
这样，碰撞规避便能通过可微信号影响训练。

30
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,785
The classifier is not needed for each deployment prediction.
每次部署推理时不需要这个分类器。

31
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:39,680
It remains a learned penalty, so hardware still needs its own safety checks.
但这仍是学习得到的惩罚项，真机仍需要自己的安全检查。

32
00:02:40,266 --> 00:02:46,126
GeoRT asks whether matching individual task vectors is enough to make control intuitive.
GeoRT 问的是：逐个匹配任务向量，是否足以让控制直观？

33
00:02:46,826 --> 00:02:52,206
The original figure shows the positions a human fingertip and an Allegro fingertip can reach.
原图展示了人手指尖与 Allegro 指尖各自能到达的位置集合。

34
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:57,986
These clouds describe fingertip workspaces, not point clouds scanned from the surface of a hand.
这些点集表示指尖工作空间，不是扫描手表面得到的点云。

35
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:02,806
Their shapes differ, so shifting and scaling alone cannot align every region well.
两者形状不同，因此平移和缩放无法让所有区域都很好地对齐。

36
00:03:03,206 --> 00:03:07,851
GeoRT learns a nonlinear mapping using several geometric criteria instead.
GeoRT 因而使用多种几何准则，学习一个非线性映射。

37
00:03:07,866 --> 00:03:13,706
The goal is predictable motion throughout the workspace, not just a visually similar still frame.
目标是在整个工作空间里响应可预测，而不只是某一帧看着相似。

38
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:20,833
For each finger, a small neural network maps human fingertip coordinates to robot joint positions.
对每根手指，一个小型神经网络把人体指尖坐标映射成机器人关节位置。

39
00:03:21,413 --> 00:03:26,793
During training, forward kinematics turns those joints back into robot fingertip coordinates.
训练时，正向运动学再把这些关节角变回机器人指尖坐标。

40
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:32,253
The geometric losses are measured there, in positions and relationships we can compare.
几何损失就在这些可比较的位置和相互关系上计算。

41
00:03:32,693 --> 00:03:37,113
Their gradients travel backward through the robot model to adjust the network weights.
损失的梯度穿过机器人模型，反向调整网络权重。

42
00:03:37,353 --> 00:03:42,098
At inference, the mapper predicts joints directly, without repeating the training loop.
推理时，映射器直接预测关节角，不再重复整个训练循环。

43
00:03:42,113 --> 00:03:47,613
A new target hand needs its model and suitable training, not just renamed output joints.
新的目标手需要相应模型和训练，而不只是给输出关节改名。

44
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:54,902
Two GeoRT objectives answer different questions, as this original illustration makes clear.
这张原论文示意图，把 GeoRT 的两个目标分得很清楚。

45
00:03:55,422 --> 00:04:00,642
Motion preservation asks whether small human movements produce consistent robot directions.
运动保持关心：人体的小幅移动，是否让机器人沿一致方向移动。

46
00:04:01,182 --> 00:04:05,502
Coverage asks how much of the robot fingertip workspace the mapping actually uses.
空间覆盖关心：映射实际利用了多少机器人指尖工作空间。

47
00:04:06,022 --> 00:04:10,362
A mapper can preserve direction while compressing every gesture into a tiny region.
一个映射可能保持方向，却把所有手势都压缩在很小的区域里。

48
00:04:10,742 --> 00:04:15,507
Conversely, widely distributed outputs can cover space while responding unpredictably.
反过来，输出分布很广、覆盖充分，也可能让响应难以预测。

49
00:04:15,522 --> 00:04:21,582
Optimizing both exposes this tradeoff rather than assuming that visual similarity already solves it.
同时优化这两个目标，才能显式处理这种权衡，而不是认为看起来相似就足够。

50
00:04:22,067 --> 00:04:26,887
Imagine moving your fingertip five millimeters in two different starting poses.
设想从两个不同的起始手势出发，都把指尖移动五毫米。

51
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:33,267
If one produces almost nothing and the other produces a sudden jump, control feels inconsistent.
如果一次几乎没反应，另一次却突然跳动，控制就会显得不一致。

52
00:04:33,707 --> 00:04:39,547
GeoRT calls for a flatter mapping, meaning that local sensitivity changes less across the space.
GeoRT 希望映射更平坦，也就是局部灵敏度在不同位置变化更小。

53
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:45,847
Its loss discourages rapid changes in that response, using nearby perturbed inputs during training.
训练时，它用附近扰动的输入，惩罚响应灵敏度的剧烈变化。

54
00:04:46,227 --> 00:04:50,872
This is a property of the spatial mapping, not simply smoothing successive video frames.
这是空间映射的性质，不只是把连续视频帧滤得更平滑。

55
00:04:50,887 --> 00:04:55,947
Our response curve is a teaching illustration; it is not a measured robot benchmark.
这里的响应曲线是教学示意，不是实测机器人性能数据。

56
00:04:56,593 --> 00:05:02,433
Pinching adds a relationship between fingers that separate motion directions cannot fully express.
捏合引入了手指之间的关系，单独约束移动方向无法充分表达它。

57
00:05:03,093 --> 00:05:07,793
When human fingertips approach, the robot fingertips should support a similar pinch.
当人体指尖靠近时，机器人指尖也应能形成类似捏合。

58
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:13,113
The original comparison shows missing pinch capability when the workspace is poorly used.
原论文对比图显示：工作空间利用不足时，一些捏合能力会缺失。

59
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:18,813
GeoRT combines pinch correspondence with its other geometric goals and a self-collision penalty.
GeoRT 把捏合对应、其他几何目标以及自碰撞惩罚结合起来。

60
00:05:19,313 --> 00:05:24,098
None of these inputs directly describes the cup's friction, weight, or required holding force.
但这些输入都没有直接描述杯子的摩擦、重量或所需保持力。

61
00:05:24,113 --> 00:05:28,673
So matching a pinch gesture and successfully lifting a cup remain different tests.
因此，匹配捏合手势，与真正把杯子提起来，仍然是两种测试。

62
00:05:29,282 --> 00:05:35,382
AnyDexRT questions whether the human should control every region the robot can mechanically reach.
AnyDexRT 进一步问：人是否必须控制机器人机械上能到达的每个区域？

63
00:05:35,842 --> 00:05:41,342
In the original figure, the robot space contains redundant regions that distort the correspondence.
原图中，机器人空间包含一些会扭曲对应关系的冗余区域。

64
00:05:41,982 --> 00:05:46,682
Partial Chamfer matching encourages valid targets without covering all robot-only regions.
部分 Chamfer 匹配鼓励目标有效，却不强求覆盖全部机器人特有区域。

65
00:05:47,422 --> 00:05:52,742
Distance preservation reduces distortion; local motion consistency compares local directions.
距离保持减少形变；局部运动一致性比较局部方向。

66
00:05:53,482 --> 00:05:58,487
These choices change what a good mapping means, rather than merely making the same optimizer faster.
这些选择改变的是“什么叫好映射”，而不只是把同一个优化器加速。

67
00:05:58,502 --> 00:06:02,862
The figure should be read from missing constraints toward the combined objective.
阅读这张图时，应从缺失约束的情况，逐步看到组合后的目标。

68
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:09,090
Several mappings satisfy those rules while placing gestures in different robot regions.
多个映射可能都满足规则，却把手势放进不同的机器人区域。

69
00:06:09,590 --> 00:06:15,170
AnyDexRT uses a small set of paired human and robot anchors to select a useful correspondence.
AnyDexRT 用少量配对的人体与机器人锚点，选择有用的对应关系。

70
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:20,390
The original figure shows lateral rotation and bending as two example anchor families.
原论文图用横向转动与弯曲，展示两类锚点动作。

71
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:25,730
The operator imitates reference gestures, and interpolation expands the collected anchor set.
操作者模仿参考手势，再通过插值扩充采集到的锚点集合。

72
00:06:26,170 --> 00:06:30,235
Calibration-free does not mean data-free, training-free, or free of human involvement.
免标定不等于不需要数据、不需要训练，或没有人工参与。

73
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:35,670
The anchors express preferred control correspondence, not unique ground truth for every task.
锚点表达的是偏好的控制对应关系，不是所有任务中唯一的真值。

74
00:06:36,236 --> 00:06:42,436
AnyDexRT addresses sensor errors: a real pinch may still appear separated in measurements.
AnyDexRT 处理传感器误差：真实捏合在测量里可能仍然分开。

75
00:06:43,496 --> 00:06:47,796
A learned classifier estimates pinch intent from the thumb and another fingertip.
学习得到的分类器，利用拇指和另一根手指的指尖位置估计捏合意图。

76
00:06:48,076 --> 00:06:52,636
That prediction refines the mapped targets before they are converted into joint commands.
这个预测会先修正映射目标，再把它们转换为关节指令。

77
00:06:52,896 --> 00:06:58,276
The diagram separates the fingertip mapper, contact refinement, and final inverse mapping.
图中把指尖映射、接触修正和最终逆映射清楚地分开了。

78
00:06:58,796 --> 00:07:03,901
This classifier is not a tactile sensor measuring whether the robot is gripping the actual object.
这个分类器不是触觉传感器，不会直接测量机器人是否真正握住了物体。

79
00:07:03,916 --> 00:07:08,776
Its demonstrated benefits still depend on the tracking inputs and hardware used in the study.
它展示的收益，仍然依赖研究中采用的追踪输入与硬件条件。

80
00:07:09,305 --> 00:07:15,105
For a fair comparison, hold the hand model, tracking input, and control stack fixed.
公平比较时，要固定手模型、追踪输入和控制系统。

81
00:07:15,445 --> 00:07:21,065
Separate mapping and camera latency, then check direction, coverage, pinching, and collisions.
把映射延迟与摄像头延迟分开，再检查方向、覆盖、捏合和碰撞。

82
00:07:22,445 --> 00:07:27,905
GeoRT reports kilohertz mapping; AnyDexRT measures speeds within its own protocol.
GeoRT 报告千赫兹映射；AnyDexRT 则在自己的协议里测量速度。

83
00:07:28,325 --> 00:07:31,805
Those numbers should not be combined into a universal speed ranking.
这些数字不能混合成一个通用速度排行榜。

84
00:07:32,145 --> 00:07:37,965
If mapping is intuitive but the object slips, first investigate sensing, contact, and control.
如果映射已经直观，但物体仍会滑落，应先检查感知、接触与控制。

85
00:07:38,665 --> 00:07:43,645
Changing the neural mapper cannot supply physical feedback missing elsewhere in the system.
更换神经映射器，不能补上系统其他部分缺失的物理反馈。
